---
const points = [
  {
    title: 'Tenant isolation at the database layer',
    body: 'Every query runs scoped to its tenant, enforced by Postgres row-level security — not just checked in application code. Defense-in-depth, not a single point of failure.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Every upload is scanned before it’s trusted',
    body: 'Documents are queued for virus scanning on upload. If the scanner is unreachable, the scan is left pending rather than silently skipped or blocking the case — honest state, not a false pass.',
  },
];
---

<section id="security" class="bg-surface-muted py-24 sm:py-32">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6">
    <div class="reveal max-w-2xl">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold text-ink sm:text-4xl">Built multi-tenant, not multi-tenant-shaped.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal mt-12 grid gap-10 border-t border-border-strong pt-10 sm:grid-cols-2 sm:gap-16">
      {
        points.map((p) => (
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-ink">{p.title}</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink">{p.body}</p>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>

    <p class="reveal mt-10 border-t border-border-strong pt-6 text-sm text-ink">
      All of it lands in an audit trail that's only ever appended to — never edited, never deleted.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
